<!-- Parameter file used by tests.stellar_populations.exe.

     Its only purpose is to declare the elements whose yields are tracked individually. `Abundances_Initialize` is a
     `nodeComponentInitializationTask`, so it reads `elementsToTrack` from this file when the test calls
     `Node_Components_Initialize`. Without it `elementsCount` is zero, only the total metal yield exists, and the
     per-element half of the test has nothing to compare.

     Carbon, oxygen and iron are chosen because between them they exercise both contributions to a yield. Oxygen and
     carbon come overwhelmingly from massive stars, and so from the isolated-star term which is restricted to stars
     that have evolved off the main sequence; iron is dominated by Type Ia supernovae, and so by the term that is
     deliberately *not* restricted in that way. All three have yields in the Portinari, Chiosi & Bressan (1998) and
     Heger & Woosley (2002) tables of the standard compilation, and in the Nomoto et al. (1997) Type Ia yields, so no
     assertion is made against a table of zeros.

     No node components or physics classes are declared. The defaults are what the test used before this file existed,
     and the assertions on the total metal yield are unchanged by its introduction.
  -->
<parameters>
  <formatVersion>2</formatVersion>
  <lastModified revision="f88a96423e21da1fe340565b2036399633246e13" time="2026-10-22T05:48:31"/>

  <elementsToTrack value="C O Fe"/>
</parameters>
